      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "CLIPTextEncode",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.3.34"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Photorealistic scientific rover footage, natural Mars daylight. A dust-covered RH-01 Pathfinder moves slowly and deliberately over rough, wild, unprepared rust-red Martian terrain: loose granular regolith, angular rocks, scattered stones, subtle wind-carved undulations, and an uninterrupted natural horizon. Preserve the reference vehicle silhouette exactly: low warm-white rectangular body with restrained muted-red panels, dark flat instrument deck, short central stereo-camera mast, exactly six broad open-mesh wheels with believable articulated suspension, and one small front-centre contact arm fully retracted and secured in its shallow travel cradle. Continuous physical motion: all six wheels visibly rotate and compress into the soil, suspension responds to stones, small grains shift beside the tires, and two clean parallel wheel tracks are continuously formed in the regolith behind the rover. Stable low three-quarter tracking camera, physically plausible scale, restrained dust, detailed real-world materials, documentary-grade realism."
      ],
      "color": "#232",
      "bgcolor": "#353"
    },
